METHOD ABSORPTION, NOT GENERIC SCHEDULER REPLACEMENT. FreeToken derives q*=m*B_P/B_H for MoE cache misses under specific assumptions: both branches consume the same host-memory source, PCIe fills and CPU expert execution run concurrently, expert item size is comparable, and B_P/B_H are empirically measured on the deployed shapes.

Represent this as a bounded PartnerMethod attached to PhysicalDerivation/ResourceWeather:
- inputs: miss cardinality m, measured pinned-transfer bandwidth B_P, measured host expert-processing bandwidth B_H, expert bytes S, cache capacity/residency, hardware/profile evidence;
- output: a PhysicalTaskPlan partition (fill set F, CPU set C), never semantic authority;
- validity tied to hardware, driver/runtime, model representation, precision, CPU kernel, NUMA/core placement, memory pressure, and measurement timestamp;
- re-profile or cool when ResourceWeather changes beyond calibration bounds;
- retain at least one cache fill only where the exact FreeToken policy applies, not as a universal theorem.

Then search existing Bonfyre methods for other two-branch shared-resource decisions that can reuse the abstract measured balancing pattern WITHOUT copying q* outside its assumptions. Promote only where the same conservation/bottleneck model is proved.
